 To achieve this in React, you can create a custom hook that fetches the field definitions from a data source (e.g., an API) and returns an object containing the field data in the desired format. Here's a basic example:
```javascript
import { useState, useEffect } from "react";

const useFieldData = (clientId, hysformId) => {
  const [fieldData, setFieldData] = useState({});

  useEffect(() => {
    const fetchData = async () => {
      const response = await fetch(
        `https://your-api.com/field-definitions?client_id=${clientId}&hysform_id=${hysformId}`
      );
      const data = await response.json();

      setFieldData(data);
    };

    fetchData();
  }, [clientId, hysformId]);

  const getFieldOptions = (fieldKey) => {
    const field = fieldData[fieldKey];

    if (!field || field.field_type !== "hysSelect") {
      return [];
    }

    const options = field.field_data.split(",").map((option) => {
      const label = option.replace(/^[0-9]+,/g, "");
      const value = option;

      return { label, value };
    });

    return options;
  };

  return { getFieldOptions };
};

export default useFieldData;
```
In this example, the `useFieldData` hook takes the client ID and hysform ID as arguments and fetches the field definitions from a custom API endpoint. It then returns an object containing a `getFieldOptions` function that takes a field key as an argument and returns an array of field options in the desired format.

To use this hook in your React components, you can simply import and call it:
```javascript
import { useFieldData } from "./useFieldData";

const App = () => {
  const { getFieldOptions } = useFieldData(207, 638);

  const genderOptions = getFieldOptions("en_gender");
  const booleanOptions = getFieldOptions("en_test_field_boolea");

  return (
    <div>
      <h2>Gender:</h2>
      <select>
        {genderOptions.map((option) => (
          <option key={option.value} value={option.value}>
            {option.label}
          </option>
        ))}
      </select>

      <h2>Test Field boolean:</h2>
      <select>
        {booleanOptions.map((option) => (
          <option key={option.value} value={option.value}>
            {option.label}
          </option>
        ))}
      </select>
    </div>
  );
};

export default App;
```
In this example, the `App` component uses the `useFieldData` hook to fetch the field definitions for the specified client ID and hysform ID. It then calls the `getFieldOptions` function to get the options for the "en\_gender" and "en\_test\_field\_boolea" fields, and renders them as select elements.

