```
\documentclass{article}

\usepackage{graphicx}

\begin{document}

\begin{center}
  \includegraphics[width=0.45\textwidth]{logo1.png}
  \hspace{0.1\textwidth}
  \includegraphics[width=0.45\textwidth]{logo2.png}
\end{center}

\end{document}
```
In this example, we use the `center` environment to center the logos horizontally, and the `includegraphics` command to include the logos as images. The `width` option is used to set the width of the images to 0.45 of the text width (`0.45\textwidth`), which makes them equal width. The `hspace` command is used to add padding between the images.

You can adjust the padding by changing the value of `\hspace`. In this example, we've added 0.1 times the text width as padding between the images.

You will need to replace `logo1.png` and `logo2.png` with the actual file names of your logos.

 Sure, here's an example code snippet that uses the VirusTotal API to check if a website is a phishing site or not and displays the result in a Bootstrap alert component:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
	<title>Phishing Site Detector</title>
	<script src="https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.6.0.min.js"></script>
	<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/bootstrap/5.3.0-alpha1/css/bootstrap.min.css">
	<script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/bootstrap/5.3.0-alpha1/js/bootstrap.min.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
	<div class="container">
		<h1>Phishing Site Detector</h1>
		<form>
			<div class="form-group">
				<label for="url">Enter URL:</label>
				<input type="url" class="form-control" id="url" name="url">
			</div>
			<button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Check</button>
		</form>
		<div id="result"></div>
	</div>

	<script>
		$(document).ready(function() {
			$('#result').html('');
			$('#result').append('<div class="alert alert-info" role="alert">Loading...</div>');
			$('#result').append('<div class="spinner-border text-primary" role="status">');
			$('#result').append('<span class="sr-only">Loading...</span>');

			$('form').submit(function(event) {
				event.preventDefault();
				$('#result').html('');
				$('#result').append('<div class="alert alert-info" role="alert">Loading...</div>');
				$('#result').append('<div class="spinner-border text-primary" role="status">');
				$('#result').append('<span class="sr-only">Loading...</span>');

				var url = $('#url').val();

				$.ajax({
					url: 'https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/urls/' + url,
					type: 'GET',
					headers: {
						'x-apikey': 'your_api_key'
					},
					success: function(response) {
						if (response.data.urls[0].status == 'malicious') {
							$('#result').append('<div class="alert alert-danger" role="alert">This website is a phishing site.</div>');
						} else {
							$('#result').append('<div class="alert alert-info" role="alert">This website is safe.</div>');
						}
					},
					error: function(jqXHR, textStatus, errorThrown) {
						$('#result').append('<div class="alert alert-danger" role="alert">Error: ' + textStatus + '</div>');
					},
					complete: function() {
						$('#result').append('<div class="spinner-border text-primary" role="status">');
						$('#result').append('<span class="sr-only">Loading...</span>');
					}
				});
			});
		});
	</script>
</body>
</html>
```
In this code, we first create a form with a URL input field and a submit button. We then use jQuery to make an AJAX request to the VirusTotal API with the URL entered by the user. If the URL is deemed safe, we display a green alert message. If the URL is deemed malicious, we display a red alert message.

Note that you will need to replace `'your_api_key'` with your own VirusTotal API key. Additionally, this code assumes that you have included the required CSS and JavaScript files for Bootstrap.

